# Opt-in: ignore everything, then allow only what the image build needs. This
# keeps the build context small — everything else (visualise/, data/, target/,
# docs/) is uploaded to the builder on every deploy otherwise.
*

# The Rust workspace `cargo build --release -p server` compiles, plus the static
# assets the runtime image copies from crates/server/static. Every member's
# manifest is needed to resolve the workspace, so the whole tree is allowed and
# the generated parts are taken back out below.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates

# The crossings a browser fetches, which the builder copies into the static dir. The only
# part of the store a deploy needs: everything else it holds is read by a query, not served.
!data/medallion/gold/artifact=crossings

# What the tree carries but the build makes for itself. The uv environments alone
# are 1.2 GB, and the wasm is written by the builder stage.
crates/**/.venv
crates/**/target
crates/**/__pycache__
crates/**/.pytest_cache
crates/server/static/wasm
crates/server/static/crossings.json
